# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# .gitignore
#
# NOTE ON GENERATED OUTPUTS
# -------------------------
# The datasets, figures and report in this repository ARE the deliverable, so
# they are deliberately committed rather than ignored. A visitor browsing the
# repo on GitHub should be able to see the figures, read the report and
# inspect the processed tables without cloning or running anything.
#
# The one exception is figures/*.pdf. GitHub's blob viewer cannot preview
# Matplotlib-generated PDFs (it shows "Unable to render code block"), which
# makes a browsing visitor think something is broken. The 400 dpi PNGs render
# perfectly inline and carry the same content, and the pipeline is seeded, so
# `python scripts/analysis.py` regenerates the vector PDFs byte-for-byte
# whenever they are needed for print or journal submission.
#
# Everything below is genuine build residue, not output.
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Vector figure exports -- regenerated by scripts/analysis.py (see note above)
figures/*.pdf

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
.Python
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
.eggs/

# Virtual environments
.venv/
venv/
env/
ENV/

# Jupyter
.ipynb_checkpoints/
*/.ipynb_checkpoints/*
.jupyter/

# Testing / coverage
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
.tox/

# Editors and IDEs
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.spyproject/
.spyderproject/

# Operating system
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
Desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/

# Scratch / temporary work
scratch/
tmp/
*.tmp
*.bak
*.log
